        "parms": "# array.push, pop, insert and more — editing an array\nqueue opens holding 60 62 64. The objects that add or change elements send the reference array queue when they are done, which runs array.tolist, so the box under it always shows queue now. pop, shift and remove send the element they took instead, and that presses the button which shows queue again.\npush and pop work at the end, unshift and shift at the front: push with pop makes a stack, push with shift a queue. Each object names the array it edits, so no array travels down a cord.",
